-- title:
--   Étale coordinate and residue character at a good off-branch point
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5\le q$ and $M'\neq 0$ is an integer with $q\nmid M'$. Write $H_1:=$ `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the group of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$; $\bar F:=$ `fieldBar q M'` is the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ obtained by `laurentBaseChange` from the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$, and $\bar F_{M'}:=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the analogous base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field. For a valuation subring $A\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $\kappa_A$ denotes its residue field, `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A M'` the subfield of $\kappa_A((t))$ generated by the two $j$-series $j_q$ and $j_q(t^{M'})$, and `xHFunctionFieldC κ_A (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` the characteristic-$q$ level-$\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ function field. A `Place K F` is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, distinct from $F$ and with principal ideals; `ord`, `evalAt` and `IsRational` are its order function, its $K$-valued evaluation map, and the condition that $K$ surject onto its residue field.
--
--   The hypotheses fall into the following groups.
--
--   *Base valuation ring.* $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the set of non-units of $A$.
--
--   *Supersingular places.* $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A M'` over $\kappa_A$, and `hW` says that $W$ is exactly `ssPlaces q M' κ_A`: the places $w$ that are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the generic $j$-invariant in `ssJSet q κ_A`, the set of those $j$ for which every elliptic curve with that $j$-invariant has no non-zero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   *Reduction of the level-$M'$ field.* `hle` is the inclusion $\bar F_{M'}\le\bar F$. $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ on $\bar F_{M'}$ with values in `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A M'`: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\bar F_{M'}$ meeting $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal and which is compatible with $A\to\kappa_A$, a scaling axiom producing for each $f\neq0$ a constant $c$ with $c\cdot f$ integral of non-zero residue, together with a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisors. `hR₀` requires that every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ lies in $\bar F_{M'}$ is an element of $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ whose residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa_A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   *Igusa rings.* $\zeta$ is an element of `Idx q`, a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ assigns a valuation subring of $\bar F$ to each point of [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21), the projective line over $\mathbb Z/q$. `hIg_inf` describes $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ as a Gauss ring: $f\in O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ if and only if there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ non-zero and $f\cdot y=x$. `hIg` requires that each line $\ell$ be of the form $\mathrm{redQ}(\gamma)\cdot\infty$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the preimage of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj` that $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ be injective; `hIg_perm` that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ the operation of pulling back along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$.
--
--   *Supersingular rings.* $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ assigns a valuation subring of $\bar F$ to each $s\in W$. `hSS_A` says that a constant $x\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ exactly when $x\in A$. `hSS_over` says that if $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ has non-negative order at every place of $\bar F_{M'}$ at which $j_q$ has non-negative order, and if $R_0.\mathrm{residue}(f)$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, then the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}(f))$ the difference of that image and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$. `hSS_fix` says each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$. `hSS_tr` provides, for each $s$, an element $t\in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ with $t-a$ a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a\in A$.
--
--   *Regular prolongation.* $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ on $\bar F$ with values in `xHFunctionFieldC κ_A (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, that is, a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\bar F$ meeting $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in $A$ together with a surjective residue map onto that characteristic-$q$ field with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A\to\kappa_A$, and satisfying the same scaling axiom. `hR` identifies $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$, and `hR₀O` says that $f\in\bar F_{M'}$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if its image in $\bar F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$.
--
--   *Ramification data.* $\pi\in A$ satisfies $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$.
--
--   *Small field of constants.* $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lies in $A$; the ring $A\cap k_0$ (the preimage of $A$ in $k_0$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field; `hκ` requires every $a\in A$ to be congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0\cap A$.
--
--   *Auxiliary prime.* $\ell$ is a prime with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\neq q$, $\ell\nmid M'$; $\zeta_0\in k_0$ is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; $\varpi_t\in k_0\cap A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   *Finite layer.* $K_1$ is a finite extension of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $A_1$ a valuation subring of $K_1$ with $x\in A_1$ if and only if $x\in A$; $A_1$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   With $\bar F$ made a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion quantifies over all intermediate fields $F_0$ of $\bar F/k_0$ subject to four conditions: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the constants $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of $\bar F$; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $K'$-linearly independent family $c_0,\dots,c_{m-1}$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is linearly independent over the compositum $k_0(K')\cdot F_0$ in the sense that $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ with all $a_i$ in that compositum forces all $a_i=0$; and $F_0$ contains every element of $\bar F$ whose Laurent expansion has rational coefficients.
--
--   Put $T_1:=$ the compositum inside $\bar F$ of $k_0$-adjoined image of $K_1$ with $F_0$. The assertion further quantifies over an $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map is the inclusion $K_1\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}\to\bar F$, and over an element $j_1\in T_1$ which, viewed in $\bar F$, is the image under `hle` of the $q$-expansion $j_q$, with $j_1\neq0$. Let $\mathfrak X:=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout gluing $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A_1[j_1]$ in $T_1$ to $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$, with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$.
--
--   Four auxiliary predicates are introduced. For $x\in\mathfrak X$ and $f\in T_1$, `InStalk x f` says that for every point $y$ of either chart lying over $x$ there are $g,h$ in the corresponding chart algebra with $h\notin y$ and $fh=g$; `InMax x f` is the same with the extra requirement $g\in y$. `Centred P x`, for a place $P$ of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, says that $P$ is rational and that every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation subring of $P$, has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$, and has $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ less than $1$ precisely when `InMax x f` holds; this predicate does not occur in the conclusion. `GoodPt x` is the conjunction of: `toBase` sends $x$ to the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$; every $y$ with $x\rightsquigarrow y$ equals $x$; for every $y$ in either chart over $x$, every chart element whose image in $\bar F$ is a non-unit of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in $y$; and for every $y$ in the finite chart over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j_1)$ does not lie in `ssJSet q Ω`. `Reads x Q`, for a place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC κ_A (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, says that every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, has $R.\mathrm{residue}(f)$ in the valuation subring of $Q$, and has $R.\mathrm{residue}(f)$ a non-unit there exactly when `InMax x f` holds. `OffBranch x` says that for every line $\ell\neq\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ and every $y$ in either chart over $x$ there is a chart element not in $y$ whose image in $\bar F$ is a non-unit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$.
--
--   The conclusion is: for every $x\in\mathfrak X$ and every place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC κ_A (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` over $\kappa_A$ such that `GoodPt x`, `OffBranch x` and `Reads x Q` hold, there exist a subring $S\subseteq\bar F$, a ring homomorphism $\varphi:A_1[X]\to S$ and a ring homomorphism $\chi:S\to\kappa_A$ with the following properties.
--
--   First, $S$ is exactly the stalk: $f\in\bar F$ belongs to $S$ if and only if $f\in T_1$ and `InStalk x f`. Second, for $f\in S$, $\chi(f)=0$ if and only if `InMax x f`. Third, the map $A_1\to\kappa_A$ sending $a$ to the residue of $a$ viewed in $A$ is surjective. Fourth, for every $a\in A_1$ the image of $a$ in $\bar F$ lies in $S$; fifth, $\varphi(C\,a)$ equals that image; sixth, $\chi(\varphi(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in $\kappa_A$; seventh, $\chi(\varphi(X))=0$. Eighth, $S$ carries a local-ring structure for which $\ker\chi$ is its maximal ideal. Ninth, $\varphi$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type. Tenth, every $f\in T_1$ can be written as a quotient of elements of $S$: there are $g,h\in S$ with $h\neq0$ and $fh=g$. Eleventh, every element of $S$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and for every uniformiser $\varpi$ of $A_1$ and every $f\in S$, the element $f$ lies in the maximal ideal of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if $\varphi(C\,\varpi)$ divides $f$ in $S$. Twelfth, for every $f\in S$ the residue $R.\mathrm{residue}(f)$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and its image in the residue field of $Q$ is the image of $\chi(f)$ under $\kappa_A\to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$. Thirteenth, $\varphi(X)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and $Q.\mathrm{ord}(R.\mathrm{residue}(\varphi(X)))=1$.
--
--   Compared with the general smooth-point presentation [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.exists_subring_etaleCoordinate_residueChar_iff_charts_of_smooth_of_isDiscreteValuationRing`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.exists_subring_etaleCoordinate_residueChar_iff_charts_of_smooth_of_isDiscreteValuationRing), the present conclusion does not assert that the maximal ideal of $S$ is generated by $\varphi(C\,\varpi)$ and $\varphi(X)$, nor surjectivity of $\chi$; it adds instead the surjectivity of $A_1\to\kappa_A$, the divisibility criterion for the maximal ideal of $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the compatibility of $\chi$ with the residue map of $Q$, and the statement that $\varphi(X)$ has order $1$ at $Q$.
--
--   This is the per-point step in the construction of the smooth Igusa base model: at a closed point of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model that lies on the $\infty$-Igusa component, avoids the other Igusa branches and has non-supersingular $j$-invariant, it presents the local ring as a formally smooth, essentially finite type $A_1[X]$-algebra whose coordinate $\varphi(X)$ is a uniformiser at the place $Q$ read off by the regular prolongation $R$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks), where such stalks supply the residue discs attached to the places $Q$.
